# The apex "cyphar.com" project is a tiny second Cloudflare Pages project (this
# directory, verbatim, with no build step) whose only jobs are:
#
#  1. Serving the /.well-known/* files checked in here;
#  2. Bouncing the rest of /.well-known/* to dot.cyphar.com;
#  3. Redirecting everything else to www.cyphar.com.
#
# Pages _redirects cannot match on hostname, which is why this cannot live in
# the www project's _redirects (it would loop).

# Masking: every file checked into apex/.well-known/ needs a matching
# self-rewrite (200) rule here, because redirects beat assets on Pages and the
# /.well-known/* splat below would otherwise shadow them. KEEP IN SYNC with
# the directory contents (scripts/check-apex.sh enforces this). These
# files must be served -- not redirected -- because browsers require every hop
# of a redirect chain to pass the CORS check, but 3xx responses here carry no
# _headers (and so no Access-Control-Allow-Origin).

# Mask any /.well-known/ rules we want to publish from the CF Pages. Redirects
# are handled before serving assets so these rules need to be first to mask the
# later catch-all rules.
/.well-known/matrix/client  /.well-known/matrix/client  200
/.well-known/matrix/server  /.well-known/matrix/server  200

# ACME challenges go to dot.cyphar.com. Cloudflare does force HTTPS before we
# get to this redirect but the ACME HTTP-01 validator is okay with that.
/.well-known/acme-challenge/*  http://dot.cyphar.com/.well-known/acme-challenge/:splat  302

# Anything else under /.well-known/* falls through to dot.cyphar.com.
/.well-known/*  https://dot.cyphar.com/.well-known/:splat  302

# And everything else goes to www.cyphar.com.
/*  https://www.cyphar.com/:splat  302
